ard now we have time  for one more question  but i do want to reiterate to our  audience and we've had so many questions  come in  that those questions we did not answer  live today and those questions that are  submitted during our on demand period  will be addressed by our speakers via  the email address you provided  at the time of registration dr steingart  our last question for the day  how much average power is required  for multi-photon tpef shg  images acquired with picosecond pulses  okay that's a great question because we  get this question a lot  there seems to be a conception that  two-photon fluorescence microscopy is  only possible with femtosecond pulses  but of course that is not true the  picosecond pulses  yes they are longer and therefore they  contain a lower peak power  but they are still able to excite such  multiphoton fluorescence processes quite  efficiently not quite as efficiently as  femtosecond pulses  but still quite okay and so it turns out  that  the powers that we use for coherent  raman scattering  microscopy are actually perfectly  suitable to excite  second harmonic generation signals and  or  two photon fluorescence signals at the  same time so  it rarely occurs that we have to change  laser settings between acquiring the  cohere  drama data and acquiring these  additional  multi-photon modalities so these can  typically be taken in the same  image run  thank you again dr spycard do you have  any final comments for our audience  i thank everyone for their um attendance  it looks like a lot of people were in  the audience we're really excited to  have been able to convey some of our  interesting  research and applications to you  and hope to hear more questions from you  as  as they come to you thank you again  i would like to once again thank our  speakers dr weyman  and dr volker schweighardt for their  time today and for their important  research  i'd also like to thank the audience for  joining us and for their interesting  questions  we would also like to thank our sponsor  leica microsystems  for underwriting today's educational  webcast  this webcast can be viewed on demand and  laborats will alert you via email when  it's available for replay  we encourage you to share that email  with your colleagues who may have missed  today's live event  thank you for joining us and we hope to  see you again soon  have a great day
 

